  "questions": [
    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-127920",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations",
      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=-1 \\\\ 3y-x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The lines $2x-2y=-1$ and $3y-x=1$ intersect at infinitely many  points\n- The coefficient matrix is not  invertible\n- The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "III only"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II only"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "III only",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
